  "worked_solution": "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta (\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta +\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta })+{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }+{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta +\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }}+{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta +1+{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & =1+({cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta ) \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta =1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta (\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta +\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta })+{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta =2.\n$$",
